{"id": "EUVD-2026-101228", "enisaUuid": "b30b8fd7-b8c2-3e4a-853b-d4e26f1a7307", "description": "xlsxio through 0.2.37 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in main_sheet_get_sheetfile_expat_callback_element_start() in lib/xlsxio_read.c that allows attackers to crash applications via crafted files. Attackers can supply a .xlsx file whose workbook.xml.rels contains a worksheet Relationship lacking an Id attribute, crashing the process when xlsxioread_sheet_open() is called.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T20:43:54", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/brechtsanders/xlsxio/issues/151", "https://github.com/brechtsanders/xlsxio/blob/0.2.37/lib/xlsxio_read.c#L851-L866", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/xlsxio-relationship-missing-id-null-deref", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xlsxio-through-0.2.37-null-pointer-dereference-via-worksheet-relationship-without-id"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6j5v-fg26-wg57", "CVE-2026-110600"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "35cd0d3f-548f-359a-abdb-6d3fdf22081b", "product": {"name": "xlsxio", "vendor": {"name": "brechtsanders"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.2.37"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4e8d8f54-29b7-3a60-a679-dc5bec9d1379", "vendor": {"name": "brechtsanders"}}], "isExploited": false}